From: RG35XX Java Platform
Task: RGJ-RC1-011CC
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: composite RG35XX bitmap text through drawRGB

Device evidence from RC1-011CB shows the fixed-cell glyphs are visible and the
MIDlet/input loop remains healthy, but direct framebuffer writes produce severe
vertical stripes/pixel corruption. Keep the Java2D glyph bypass, but never let
the text helper touch canvasData. Build an isolated transparent ARGB bitmap and
composite it through PlatformGraphics.drawRGB(processAlpha=true), a path already
validated by the comprehensive device test.

--- a/src/org/recompile/mobile/PlatformGraphics.java
+++ b/src/org/recompile/mobile/PlatformGraphics.java
@@ -853,7 +853,19 @@
 			if((anchor & Graphics.BOTTOM)>0) { y = y-height; }
 			if((anchor & Graphics.BASELINE)>0) { y = y-ascent; }
 
-			gc.drawString(str, x, y);
+			if(RG35XXPlatformProfile.isActive() && !Mobile.isDoJa)
+			{
+				final int bitmapWidth = RG35XXBitmapText.width(str);
+				if(bitmapWidth > 0)
+				{
+					final int[] raster = RG35XXBitmapText.render(str, getColor());
+					drawRGB(raster, 0, bitmapWidth, x, y - ascent,
+						bitmapWidth, RG35XXBitmapText.CELL_HEIGHT, true);
+				}
+			}
+			else
+			{
+				gc.drawString(str, x, y);
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
